=================================================
Sample Partition
=================================================
; @version 1.0

; This is a sample voxalfa file (.vfa), it was designed to be a simple language for composing and storing Tonic-Solfa pieces.
; It is a markup language with inline markers denoted with [<marker>]
; 
; We can divide the file into two parts:
; - Header: contains metadata and the initial parameters for the song
; - Body: contains the actual Solfa composition and lyrics, it can be divided into multiple sections with their own parameters
; 
; There are two kinds of markers:
; - K/V: they define a key/value pair ([#], [$], [^])
; - Formatters: they are immediately followed by tokens that follows a specific syntax rule ([<voice>], [<verse>])
; 
; The language supports simple data types, types without delimiters needs curly brackets {...}.
; - Strings: delimited by double quotes "..."
; - Numbers: signed integer or float
; - Boolean: true or false
; - List: a simple one dimensional list of scalar values delimited by {...}, we can think of any scalar value as a list of 1 item
; - Tokens: they represent built-in values or identifiers (notes, voices, ...)

[#] title="Hello World"
[#] author={"Foo Bar", "Jane Doe"}
[#] composer="Bob"
[#] description="Lorem Ipsum."
[#] release={2026}

[$] key={C} | bpm={100} | time={4,4} | voices={S,T,A,B}

---

; we can override the global parameters inside sections
; [$] bpm={80}

; there are also section-only parameters
[$] repeat={true}

[^] p={1} | cre={3,6}

[S] d : r ! m : f | `s : l` ! t : - | da+1 : - ! ~ : ~
[T] d : r ! m : f | `s : l` ! t : - | da+1 : - ! ~ : ~
[A] d : r ! m : f | `s : l` ! t : - | da+1 : - ! ~ : ~
[B] d : r ! m : f | `s : l` ! t : - | da+1 : - ! ~ : ~

[1] do `re` mi\(f a) so la ti_i do_o. ~ ~ <\>
[2] do `re` mi\(f a) so la ti_i do_o. ~ ~ <\> ; scream

--

; more sections...

----

